From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ncrypt: protection descriptors, NCryptProtectSecret and NCryptUnprotectSecret, streams

NCryptCreateProtectionDescriptor parses a descriptor string (LOCAL=user,
LOCAL=machine, LOCAL=logon and SID=... rules joined by AND or OR, not mixed;
a bad string, a mixed one or an unknown flag is NTE_INVALID_PARAMETER,
SDDL=, CERTIFICATE= and WEBCREDENTIALS= rules are refused) into a handle that
NCryptCloseProtectionDescriptor closes and NCryptGetProtectionDescriptorInfo
reads back (caller's allocator or LocalAlloc). NCryptProtectSecret protects
the data with DPAPI, for the user or, without a user rule, the machine, with
the descriptor as entropy, and puts the descriptor in the blob;
NCryptUnprotectSecret checks the rules against the caller's token (SID rules
by membership, AND needs all, OR any: NTE_PERM otherwise), unprotects, and
can hand back a descriptor handle. NCryptStreamOpenToProtect,
OpenToUnprotect(Ex), Update and Close collect the pieces and give the result
to the output callback with the last one. These were stubs.
---
